{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/961810-child-characters-in-regular-cofd","id":961810,"title":"Child characters in regular CofD?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-09-01T12:03:57-07:00","id":961810,"title":"Child characters in regular CofD?","content":"So the chronicle I'm putting together is going to be more <i>Stranger Things</i> than <i>Supernatural</i>. There's some obvious Stephen King influences there, and one of the common tropes in that sort of horror is the child character (who often has some kind of psychic power or at least is more sensitive to the weirdness around them). (Examples: Eleven from <i>Stranger Things</i>, Charlie from <i>Firestarter</i>, Newt from <i>Aliens</i>, Jake from the Dark Tower series, etc.) And given the kinds of characters one of the players in my group tends to play, I have a feeling that they're going to want to make a child character.<br /> <br /> Unfortunately, the only book in the nWoD/CoD that seems to address child characters (as far as I've been able to find) is Innocents, but it assumes all of the characters will be children, and isn't really compatible with other CoD games. So other than saying &quot;No, you can't play a kid, sorry&quot;, what's the best way to deal with this?<br /> <br /> A child character of between about 10 and 16 would be Size 4, and have a commensurately lower Speed and Health than an adult. But what about attributes and skills? On one hand, starting the character out with fewer dots to spend would make sense, and could be said is the price of playing a child. On the other hand, if this is playing to the trope, the kids are typically able to hold their own in a group of adults. Maybe put a cap of three dots on any attribute or skill? Since I'll be using Magic Character Beans, maybe starting the character out with fewer attribute and skill points but more MCBs would work. And I'm thinking that this should all be covered by a Condition of Child.<br /> <br /> I'd love to hear any suggestions if anyone has any ideas on how best to deal with this.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12354-who-is-matt","name":"who.is.matt","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"29"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-01T12:14:34-07:00","id":961822,"title":"","content":"So, are you just trying to model mortal characters as children, how to balance a child in a mixed group, or how to incorporate more elements in when you have to account for a child character?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-01T12:17:03-07:00","id":961825,"title":"","content":"Hey! I use child characters in all of my chronicles. Fifteen is really the age where I base it more on maturity, if they should use modified child stats or adult stats, but there's a number pattern in <b>Innocents </b>that you can extend for children over twelve, which is where that book stops. There's normally that cap of three dots for Attributes and Skills, and <b>Innocents </b>has child only Merits, including Merits like Mental/Physical/Social protegee that allow you to buy skills over three dots. I've found Innocents quite compatible, and every game I've ran since I started STing has involved child characters at all levels of influence within the campaign. I'm currently running a game with an eleven year old <b>Beast </b>Storyteller character, in fact. It can absolutely, definitely, be done, using <b>Innocents </b>for child characters in an otherwise adult CoD game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:12px\">-</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3093-hm8453a","name":"hm8453a","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3093_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"636"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-01T12:18:08-07:00","id":961827,"title":"","content":"I would use Innocents Character Creation, and then follow the rules for translating the child character into the adult world within the book (growing up). <br /> <br /> This will give an appropriate reduction in capability.<br /> <br /> If you want child characters to be just as capable as the adults for some reason, just use normal character generation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-01T12:32:55-07:00","id":961837,"title":"","content":"If you want, and the child character is supposed to be &quot;special&quot;, you could always use the existing Innocents restrictions, but make up the difference in their special traits/abilities (Supernatural Merits, Skill Tricks, etc.).<br /> <br /> Gamelines that might be applicable:<br /> Werewolf, for Wolf-Blooded. Many have that happen regardless of their age (even being born that way), according to the text in some Tells.<br /> Mage, if you want to go with a Proximus (&quot;you're a wizard, Harry!&quot;).<br /> Changeling (2E playtest preview) for Fae-Touched.<br /> Demon, for Offspring/Fractals, or even just a Demon with a child Cover (though <i>that</i> will swing the power discrepancy far in the other direction).<br /> <br /> The following are possible, if a bit dark:<br /> Vampire, either for Ghoul (come on, man, really?) or a full vampire (the Anthology had one).<br /> Changeling, for a full Changeling.<br /> Geist, if the kid made a Bargain young.<br /> Beast, for when they really <i>were </i>eaten by monster(s) in the closet/under the bed.<br /> <br /> Mummy is about the only one that isn't suitable.<br /> <br /> (Blue Books: Immortals, for Warden, Reborn, Visitor, and <i>maybe</i> Purified. Inferno, if you want to recreate the Exorcist.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-01T12:45:17-07:00","id":961845,"title":"","content":"The only thing that has struck me as not-easily-compatible in Innocents is Attributes. Skills work well with the 3-dot cap, size 4 as a base makes sense, and the child Merits are great, but for Attributes Innocents just says they're on a different scale than adults and that 5 dots in Strength (for example) means something different for a child than it does for an adult. Which makes sense and works fine for an Innocents Chronicle, but once you've got adult characters involved it seems like it would become a point of dissonance between the narrative and the mechanics. A Stregth 3, Brawl 3 11-year-old is going to be evenly matched in a grapple with a Strength 3, Brawl 3 26-year-old, despite the fact that an adult's Strength 3 is supposed to represent more muscular capability than a child's Strength 3. How do folks who use kids in their chronicles handle that?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-01T12:49:52-07:00","id":961848,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/961810-child-characters-in-regular-cofd?p=961845#post961845\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The only thing that has struck me as not-easily-compatible in Innocents is Attributes. Skills work well with the 3-dot cap, size 4 as a base makes sense, and the child Merits are great, but for Attributes Innocents just says they're on a different scale than adults and that 5 dots in Strength (for example) means something different for a child than it does for an adult. Which makes sense and works fine for an Innocents Chronicle, but once you've got adult characters involved it seems like it would become a point of dissonance between the narrative and the mechanics. A Stregth 3, Brawl 3 11-year-old is going to be evenly matched in a grapple with a Strength 3, Brawl 3 26-year-old, despite the fact that an adult's Strength 3 is supposed to represent more muscular capability than a child's Strength 3. How do folks who use kids in their chronicles handle that?</div> </div> </div> </div>I usually give additional bonuses to the adults based on the specific circumstance. It's simpler than figuring out how the scales might translate differently.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:12px\">-</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3093-hm8453a","name":"hm8453a","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3093_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"636"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-01T12:59:41-07:00","id":961855,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>hm8453a</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/961810-child-characters-in-regular-cofd?p=961848#post961848\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I usually give additional bonuses to the adults based on the specific circumstance. It's simpler than figuring out how the scales might translate differently.</div> </div> </div> </div>Makes sense. I guess you could use dice tricks like 8- and 9-Again, removing 10-again, Rote, Advanced, etc. That way you don't need to mess too much with the numbers themselves but can still put adults at an advantage.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-01T13:00:55-07:00","id":961856,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>hm8453a</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/961810-child-characters-in-regular-cofd?p=961848#post961848\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I usually give additional bonuses to the adults based on the specific circumstance. It's simpler than figuring out how the scales might translate differently.</div> </div> </div> </div>What about applying a modifier based on the Size discrepancy? -1 in this case.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-01T13:07:01-07:00","id":961857,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/961810-child-characters-in-regular-cofd?p=961856#post961856\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> What about applying a modifier based on the Size discrepancy? -1 in this case.</div> </div> </div> </div>Having grown up with a disability that affected and still affects my height, being smaller might not hurt someone in a fight. It could actually help them move in creative ways. <b>Innocents </b>discusses this, actually.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:12px\">-</span>","edited":{"userid":3093,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3093-hm8453a","user":"hm8453a","date":". 09-01-2016, 04:13 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3093-hm8453a","name":"hm8453a","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3093_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"636"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-01T15:05:38-07:00","id":961920,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>who.is.matt</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/961810-child-characters-in-regular-cofd#post961810\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So the chronicle I'm putting together is going to be more <i>Strangler Things</i> than <i>Supernatural</i>. There's some obvious Stephen King influences there, and one of the common tropes in that sort of horror is the child character (who often has some kind of psychic power or at least is more sensitive to the weirdness around them). (Examples: Eleven from <i>Stranger Things</i>, Charlie from <i>Firestarter</i>, Newt from <i>Aliens</i>, Jake from the Dark Tower series, etc.) And given the kinds of characters one of the players in my group tends to play, I have a feeling that they're going to want to make a child character.<br /> <br /> Unfortunately, the only book in the nWoD/CoD that seems to address child characters (as far as I've been able to find) is Innocents, but it assumes all of the characters will be children, and isn't really compatible with other CoD games. So other than saying &quot;No, you can't play a kid, sorry&quot;, what's the best way to deal with this?<br /> <br /> A child character of between about 10 and 16 would be Size 4, and have a commensurately lower Speed and Health than an adult. But what about attributes and skills? On one hand, starting the character out with fewer dots to spend would make sense, and could be said is the price of playing a child. On the other hand, if this is playing to the trope, the kids are typically able to hold their own in a group of adults. Maybe put a cap of three dots on any attribute or skill? Since I'll be using Magic Character Beans, maybe starting the character out with fewer attribute and skill points but more MCBs would work. And I'm thinking that this should all be covered by a Condition of Child.<br /> <br /> I'd love to hear any suggestions if anyone has any ideas on how best to deal with this.</div> </div> </div> </div>Don't make their character weaker, and don't give them a lower size, all that and the slight frame merit does is make their chacter less effective than everyone else. I am playing a 14 year old in the game I'm in. The way I'm doing it is keeping him size 5, and not putting points in strength, and stamina. I also gave him a lower presence and composure than I normally do. If I get into a situation where a kid would be at a disadvantage such as grappling with a grown man, or talking your way into a adult only area, I turn failures into dramatic failures. In the event I succeed, I will think of a creative way to discribe it, or succeed while asking my storyteller for a condition. This makes it possible for me to get a lot of beats, and makes it feel more believable. Skills aren't as much of a problem as long as they aren't too technical. Kids are sometimes quite skilled in real life anyway. Deciding to give yourself lower stats in some parts, and higher in others can make you a very effective character. No one wants to play an average kid, but playing an exceptional child character can be fun.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12094,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12094-k9ine","user":"K9ine","date":". 09-01-2016, 06:15 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12094-k9ine","name":"K9ine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12094_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"270"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-01T15:15:46-07:00","id":961924,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/961810-child-characters-in-regular-cofd?p=961822#post961822\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, are you just trying to model mortal characters as children, how to balance a child in a mixed group, or how to incorporate more elements in when you have to account for a child character?</div> </div> </div> </div>I would be trying to fit a child in a group of adults, which is why <i>Innocents</i> wouldn't work. As others have pointed out, <i>Innocents</i> uses a different scale for Attributes and Skills.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lnodiv</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/961810-child-characters-in-regular-cofd?p=961827#post961827\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would use Innocents Character Creation, and then follow the rules for translating the child character into the adult world within the book (growing up).</div> </div> </div> </div>Huh... I didn't notice the rules for aging up characters in <i>Innocents</i>. However, after looking them up, I don't think they'd really work since they're specifically intended to age the child up to an adult character. In fact, they sort of do the opposite of what I want to do.<br /> <br /> After thinking on it some more, I'm considering dealing with this one of two ways...<br /> <br /> <b>Option 1</b>: Treat it as a Condition. <br /> <br /> <u>Condition: Adolescent</u><br /> Your character is physically between about 10 and 15 years of age. The character is considered to have the Small Frame Merit. Additionally, while this Condition is in effect, any dots greater than 3 in any Physical Attribute are ignored, and the character does not benefit from 10-again on any rolls involving Physical Attributes.<br /> <i>Beat</i>: Danger or severe inhibition due to the Condition.<br /> <i>Resolution</i>: The character physically ages to an adult.<br /> <br /> This would be the easiest to deal with should I decide to do some wonky things with time shifts, and could be removed from or applied to characters easily. The character gets a free 2-dot Merit (though one that has some definite drawbacks), and can potentially gain some Beats (actually Willpower, since we'll be using MCBs). The main problem with this is that a player who knows his character is going to have this Condition could basically avoid the limitation on Physical Attributes by going Mental/Social primary (which is why I added the lack of 10-again on Physical Attribute rolls.) I'm also not sure if Dexterity should be penalized, since while kids don't have the strength or toughness of an adult, they can be pretty quick and agile.<br /> <br /> <b>Option 2</b>: Alter character creation for adolescent characters.<br /> <br /> <i>The child character must take the Small Frame Merit. The character gets 4/3/2 dots for Attributes and 9/6/3 dots for Skills, but begins play with 20 additional MCBs. These bonus MCBs cannot be spent to improve the character, and only as bonus dice or to purchase narrative elements (as per </i>Mirrors<i> p34, &quot;Cooperative World Building&quot;).</i><br /> <br /> This might better represent the physical immaturity and lack of experience of a child, as well as the trope's tendency of the &quot;kid&quot; being able to significantly influence the plot despite lacking the abilities of the adults around him. The main downside is that it's less versatile, should I want to do anything odd with the timeline of the chronicle, either narratively (such as flashbacks or flash-forwards) or as some sort of weird in-universe effect.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12354-who-is-matt","name":"who.is.matt","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"29"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-01T15:51:02-07:00","id":961938,"title":"","content":"Here's some Conditions I whipped up for playing children and teens.<br /> <br /> <u>Juvenile (Persistent)</u><br /> Your character is very young - her body and mind are still developing, putting her at a disadvantage in an adult world. Her Size and Speed are both reduced by 1, and you cannot raise any of her Skills above 3 dots. Additionally, you do not benefit from the 10-again quality on teamwork actions that involve adult characters, and adult characters gain the 8-again quality on Contested actions against her.<br /> <b>Beat:</b> Your are denied agency as a result of your age.<br /> <b>Resolution:</b> When your character reaches physical maturity.<br /> <br /> <u>Adolescent (Persistent)</u><br /> Your character is in an awkward transitionary phase of development - no longer a child, but not yet an adult, she struggles to find her place in the world. Adults tend to assume the worst in your character until she proves her maturity to them. You begin all Social Maneuvering attempts with adult characters at a Hostile impression.<br /> <b>Beat:</b> You face prejudice or discrimination as a result of your age.<br /> <b>Resolution:</b> Your character reaches developmental maturity.<br /> <br /> I figure a young child (9-12ish) would begin with Juvenile, while a young adult (17-20ish) would start with Adolescent. A Teenager (13-16ish) would get the worst of both worlds and start with both Conditions. Thoughts?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 09-01-2016, 10:02 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-01T18:05:34-07:00","id":962000,"title":"","content":"I like. They play up the rebellious / angsty teen angle a bit more than I would, but the Juvenile Condition is close to what I came up with (but called &quot;Adolescent&quot;). And I think that a Condition really is the way to go, especially if I decide to do any odd time shifts. A decade flashforward or flashback or some sort of odd time shift due to dimensional weirdness would be a lot easier to handle by just adding or removing Conditions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12354-who-is-matt","name":"who.is.matt","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"29"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-01T18:38:47-07:00","id":962013,"title":"","content":"I like the condition too. Mind if I borrow them for use in the Jim Williams Charter School Network in my Savannah write-up? one of the local mysteries is that all the occult energies flowing through the city somehow causes supernatural abilities to manafest earlier, so the city had to set up a charter school through a front company for all the kid magi, werewolf puppies, weird sin-eater kids, little changlings and spooky beastlings that crop up, along with that one ancient child prodigy mummy, currently being raised by the couple who found his tomb.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Despite the user name I am actually bigender.<br /> <br /> My Savannah Setting for CofD can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/959455-the-young-man-in-the-cafe-s-savannah-georgia-setting-writeup\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> <br /> My heroes as monster tamers rules for BtP can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/975230-heroes-as-monster-tamers-rules-ideas\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3932-the-young-man-in-the-cafe","name":"The young man in the cafe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3932_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-01T19:00:41-07:00","id":962020,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The young man in the cafe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/961810-child-characters-in-regular-cofd?p=962013#post962013\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I like the condition too. Mind if I borrow them for use in the Jim Williams Charter School Network in my Savannah write-up? one of the local mysteries is that all the occult energies flowing through the city somehow causes supernatural abilities to manafest earlier, so the city had to set up a charter school through a front company for all the kid magi, werewolf puppies, weird sin-eater kids, little changlings and spooky beastlings that crop up, along with that one ancient child prodigy mummy, currently being raised by the couple who found his tomb.</div> </div> </div> </div>Go for it! I wouldn't post it publicly if I didn't want people to use it <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-01T20:06:12-07:00","id":962042,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/961810-child-characters-in-regular-cofd?p=962020#post962020\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Go for it! I wouldn't post it publicly if I didn't want people to use it <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks, Savannah to me is a perfect place for a monster school, since it's walkable enough for kids to get around without parental help, just dangerous enough that the kids need to be somewhat street smart and has the tunnels for the school to put the classrooms for the more supernatural classes in beneath the normal part of the school. Not to mention that the city is full of shops and attractions that a supernatural child might find useful. Sin eater kids probably get most of their mementos at the many local antiques shops, Uratha pups would practice hunting at Skidaway state park and Oatland Island wildlife center, The area around the Georgia state railroad museum is the largest playground in the state, so we know what the neutral zone for the supernatural cliques is,(it has to be the neutral zone what with being a locus and a Hallow (and the only one they can use without their parents looking <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />) The mighty 8th air force museum is popular with Ugallu kids and occasionally the dumber sin eater kids will try to steal memento weapons from world war two from it (They usually fail because TFV isn't stupid), the smart sin eater kids hang out at Laurel Grove Cemetery and have secret santas there every Christmas (since the writer of the song jingle bells is buried there, but only sin-eater girl scouts are allowed near Gordon Low's grave), but the Juliet Gordon low house is off limits to non girl scouts, the supernatural scouts have some really weird merit badges, and don't ask about the special cookies....<br /> <br /> I am gonna expand this post a bit and then add it to the Savannah write-up later.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Despite the user name I am actually bigender.<br /> <br /> My Savannah Setting for CofD can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/959455-the-young-man-in-the-cafe-s-savannah-georgia-setting-writeup\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> <br /> My heroes as monster tamers rules for BtP can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/975230-heroes-as-monster-tamers-rules-ideas\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3932-the-young-man-in-the-cafe","name":"The young man in the cafe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3932_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-01T20:26:14-07:00","id":962046,"title":"","content":"Here is the version I use. <hr /><br /> <b>Child </b><b>[Persistent]</b><br /> Your character is a pre-adolescent (typically between 7-12 years of age). Character at this stage of development have several disadvantages when compared to an adult; their base size is 4, their Speed factor is 4, and any unarmed attack made against an adult or adult sized creature suffers a -2 penalty. However, the characters smaller stature works to their advantage in some situations; against adults they gain a +1 die bonus to Stealth, Breaking Free of Grapple, or when Dodging.<br /> <b>Resolution: </b>This condition is a normal part of human development and is shed over time as the character matures. However, supernatural circumstances can trap an adult in a child\u2019s body either temporarily or indefinitely.<br /> <b>Beat: </b>When the characters youth causes a significant social or physical set back (especially when dealing with adults).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1420009-the-artificer-s-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">The Artificer's Workshop</a> - A collection of Exalted Artifacts<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806809-curios-relics-and-tomes\" target=\"_blank\">Curios, Relics, and Tomes</a> - A collection of Relics (Cursed and Otherwise)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/793173-the-horror-show\" target=\"_blank\">The Horror Lab</a> - A collection of Beasts, Monsters and less definable things.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1128197-strange-places#post1128197\" target=\"_blank\">Strange Places</a> - A collection of Dark, Mysterious, and Wondrous Locations<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/993181-twilight-menagerie\" target=\"_blank\">Twilight Menagerie</a> - A collection of Ephemeral Entities","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/775-reighnhell","name":"Reighnhell","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar775_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"749"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-02T22:30:50-07:00","id":962706,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/775-reighnhell\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar775_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"775\" data-vbnamecard=\"775\">Reighnhell</a> , as always, <b>superb</b> stuff! Will steal it to my games, till devs don't do <b>Innocents</b> for 2E. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-03T07:16:29-07:00","id":962811,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/961810-child-characters-in-regular-cofd?p=962706#post962706\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Till devs don't do <b>Innocents</b> for 2E. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>From your mouth to Rich's ears, with Matt hiring Sean and I as writers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:12px\">-</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3093-hm8453a","name":"hm8453a","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3093_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom